      "instructionPlacements": {
        "learn": {
          "paragraph": "An EVENT starts a script; a FOREVER loop repeats checks; CHANGE X changes horizontal position. The teacher projects and models this exact Player script: when green flag clicked → go to x:0 y:−125 → forever {if key [right arrow] pressed? then change x by 8; if key [left arrow] pressed? then change x by −8; if x position > 215 then set x to 215; if x position < −215 then set x to −215}. Students observe how each block is located in Events, Motion, Control, Sensing and Operators. A restart must reset the same position each time.",
          "sectionId": "group_learn",
          "field": "text"
        },
        "practice": {
          "paragraph": "Teacher drags one block at a time while class predicts outcome: green flag resets position; right key increases x; left decreases x; boundaries prevent disappearing. Students arrange a paper block-flow sketch before implementing.",
          "sectionId": "group_practice",
          "field": "text"
        },
        "perform": {
          "paragraph": "Select Player only. Build the displayed reset-and-forever keyboard control. Test right, left, both stage edges, and stopping/restarting. Leave FallingObject untouched. Save the SAME project; do not duplicate it.",
          "sectionId": "group_practice",
          "field": "activity.instructions"
        }
      },
