      "instructionPlacements": {
        "learn": {
          "paragraph": "The falling script belongs to FallingObject, not Player. Exact teacher recipe: when green flag clicked → forever {go to x:(pick random −210 to 210) y:170; repeat until (y position < −175) {change y by −5; wait 0.03 seconds}}. Forever restarts the drop; repeat until ends an individual fall; random x varies each start. Keep its sprite a plain circle. Compare one loop that repeats the entire game and another loop that controls one falling trip. Change the speed cautiously and test from a known reset.",
          "sectionId": "group_practice",
          "field": "text"
        },
        "practice": {
          "paragraph": "Teacher predicts output for fixed x versus pick random, demonstrates sign of negative y, then changes only one parameter. Class identifies loop nesting and why a sprite script must be attached to the correct object.",
          "sectionId": "group_practice",
          "field": "activity.instructions"
        },
        "perform": {
          "paragraph": "Use the exact supplied FallingObject recipe, test at least five drops, verify the player still responds, and save SAME project. Keep a simple scoreboard note listing observed spawn x changes, fall direction and restart behavior.",
          "sectionId": "perform",
          "field": "steps"
        }
